{
  "requirement": "During one call to `Validator::verify`, direct reads by the criterion and\nreads served by the SDK's agent tools record inputs in the same\n`ValidationContext`. For example, if criterion code reads a test and the agent\nthen reads its helper, both node fingerprints accompany the returned answer.\nA subsequent verification starts with an empty dependency list.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "**Structural obligations.** `shared_context` requires three things:\n1. Direct reads by the criterion and reads served by the agent tools record into the same `ValidationContext` during one `Validator::verify` call.\n2. The returned answer carries those fingerprints.\n3. A later verification starts with an empty dependency list.\n\n**Single context per verify call.**\n- `crates/trust-but-verify/src/graph/runtime.rs#impl[Validator<D>]#1/fn[verify]` builds one `ValidationContext::configured(...)` per call and passes it to `criterion.execute`.\n- `crates/trust-but-verify/src/procedure.rs#impl[ValidationContext<'d, D>]#1/fn[configured]` initialises `observations` with `Default::default()`, so each verification starts empty.\n- Because a fresh context is built on every `verify` call, nothing carries over to a later verification.\n- `verify` returns `ctx.dependencies()` in `Fingerprinted`, so every recorded fingerprint accompanies the answer.\n\n**Direct reads.**\n- In `crates/trust-but-verify/src/procedure.rs#impl[ValidationContext<'d, D>]#2`, `read_snapshot` calls `prepare_read` and then `record_read`.\n- `outgoing_edges` calls `observe_edges`.\n- Both write into the context's single `observations` mutex-guarded vector.\n\n**Agent-tool reads use the same context.**\n- `crates/trust-but-verify/src/procedure.rs#impl[Ask<'a, 'd, D, R, P>]#2/fn[execute]` passes `self.ctx` to `agent.run(request, self.ctx)`.\n- The `Agent::run` trait method takes `&ValidationContext`. `crates/trust-but-verify/src/agent/configured.rs#impl[ConfiguredAgent<D>/Agent<D>]/fn[run]` forwards the same `inspection` to `ToolAgent::run`.\n- `crates/trust-but-verify/src/agent/tools.rs#impl[ToolAgent<P, T>/Agent<D>]/fn[run]` stores that reference in `GraphSession.inspection`. It also queues the prepared input fingerprints as pending dependencies.\n- `GraphSession#impl[Conversation]/fn[dispatch]` serves `read_node` and `outgoing_edges` through `inspection.prepare_read` and `inspection.prepare_edges`. It queues the observations, and it also queues dependencies from delegated tool deliveries.\n- `GraphSession#impl[Conversation]/fn[delivered]` drains the pending list into `inspection.record_read` and `inspection.observe_edges`. These are the same recording methods the direct reads use, so the observations land in the shared context.\n\n**Other checks.**\n- Reading a test and then its helper yields two `Dependency::Node` entries. `record_read` only deduplicates entries with an identical node and fingerprint.\n- I found no structural gap and no conflicting element.\n- There are no `{fixme}` acknowledgments.\n- I did not assess runtime behavior or tests, because this review is structural only.",
  "references": "2c35862fa48dbc05e8825f322f614b0f35937ab779b0239d61752080a67691e4",
